            <ArticleTitle>Cervical spine surgery and handwriting: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1043-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The 53-year-old right-handed woman underwent decompressive laminectomies and foraminotomies at the C3-C7 levels. The course of illness and postoperative recovery were documented by handwriting and MRI views, but not statistical analysis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
